Golden archive pairs (phase 7c1, spec decision 12: at most 20, saved by hand)
==========================================================================

`eval build --suite changes` reads every sub-directory here (sorted by name, first 20) as one before/after pair of a
competitor web page and turns each changed block into an unlabelled `changes` case (source `archive`, id
`changes-archive-<dir>-<n>`). Labels come from `eval label --prelabel` and the owner's CSV confirmation.

Cap (spec decision 12: 60 golden in total): at most 20 archive cases, picked round-robin across pairs, each pair's most
informative block first (money facts, then any number, then the largest text change). Scripted mutation cases fill the
rest round-robin by fixture page, then the natural v1->v2 diffs, up to 60.

Layout, one directory per pair (lowercase name, e.g. `acme-dental-specials-2025`):

  <pair>/before.html   the older snapshot (raw HTML as served by web.archive.org, `id_` URL form so no Wayback toolbar)
  <pair>/after.html    the newer snapshot of the same page
  <pair>/meta.json     { "vertical": "dental" | "hvac_plumbing",
                         "competitorName": "Acme Dental",
                         "pageUrl": "https://acme.example/specials",
                         "pageType": "specials",            (optional)
                         "beforeUrl": "https://web.archive.org/web/<ts>id_/...",
                         "afterUrl":  "https://web.archive.org/web/<ts>id_/..." }

How to save a pair:
- Pick a local dental or HVAC/plumbing competitor page with a meaningful change between two archive.org snapshots
  (price, offer, new service, area, hiring). Download each snapshot with the `id_` modifier in a browser
  (`https://web.archive.org/web/<timestamp>id_/<url>`) and save it as before.html / after.html. Do not crawl the live
  site (crawler conduct rules) and do not edit the HTML except to delete obvious tracking scripts.
- Keep files LF-only. Text passes the engine's own block extraction + alignBlocks + numeric facts, then
  `redactForModel` (contact details and person names are removed before anything is written to data/).
- Run `pnpm --filter @cs/evals eval build --suite changes` and check `pnpm --filter @cs/evals test` (the redaction scan).
